    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "T0OROUTC7",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped 'Logic Gate NOT-NAND' gate. Role in the 4-bit adder: carry-out of stage 0, copy 7 of 10: same majority(A0, B0, C0) as T0OROUT, feeding T1H2N5C4.A. The whole 4-bit adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate's truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction — there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of the A, B and Cin bits onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages — and each stage's carry-out, which must reach the next stage's several carry-in pins — are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in 'Logic Gate Half Adder').",
        "Identifier": "group_02a981298b174da38cbff01ecbf44228",
        "IdGuid": "7cfef0aa-2abf-47ca-928d-3fe7c71ddede",
        "ChildComponentGuids": [
          "1a6ddd54-6494-4e03-83ea-4c85ce8d8516",
          "9f2e3a3c-4ec9-4eb1-aeab-57bbb2d25c14",
