    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "T1OROUTC4",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped 'Logic Gate NOT-NAND' gate. Role in the 4-bit adder: carry-out of stage 1, copy 4 of 7: same majority(A1, B1, C1) as T1OROUT, feeding T2H2N5.A. The whole 4-bit adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate's truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction — there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of the A, B and Cin bits onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages — and each stage's carry-out, which must reach the next stage's several carry-in pins — are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in 'Logic Gate Half Adder').",
        "Identifier": "group_730eb5ef7a92444383217716aa9a0f64",
        "IdGuid": "93e47943-353f-411b-9ea3-1bf7edd68bcc",
        "ChildComponentGuids": [
