    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "T3H1N21",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped 'Logic Gate NOT-NAND' gate. Role in the 4-bit adder: second XOR stage of stage 3's partial sum (chain 1 of 4), Y = NAND(A3, T3H1N1A1.Y), feeding T3H1SUM1.A. The whole 4-bit adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate's truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction — there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of the A, B and Cin bits onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages — and each stage's carry-out, which must reach the next stage's several carry-in pins — are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in 'Logic Gate Half Adder').",
        "Identifier": "group_8ed845a54aeb4e9eb5dedaddcbb834b2",
        "IdGuid": "98c184e1-2aac-4a7d-9194-a7b2d4101485",
