    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "T3H1N24",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped 'Logic Gate NOT-NAND' gate. Role in the 4-bit adder: second XOR stage of stage 3's partial sum (chain 4 of 4), Y = NAND(A3, T3H1N1A4.Y), feeding T3H1SUM4.A. The whole 4-bit adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate's truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction — there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of the A, B and Cin bits onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages — and each stage's carry-out, which must reach the next stage's several carry-in pins — are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in 'Logic Gate Half Adder').",
        "Identifier": "group_61dbc032ae214f3e9432f2b3dd6d648b",
        "IdGuid": "7be834c1-f472-4667-9ea9-b723d20327ba",
        "ChildComponentGuids": [
          "91118d36-2fef-4812-ade2-e2cd69feb45f",
